# Reflick web (Vite)
#
# The API's own origin, used by production builds only. Every request becomes
# `${VITE_API_URL}/api/...`, so the web and the API can be two separate services
# (two Render projects, or Vercel + Render) with nothing but this link between them.
#
# Leave it unset to keep everything same-origin on `/api` - that relies on a host
# rewrite (see render.yaml) forwarding /api/* to the API service instead.
#
# Local dev ignores this value: `vite dev` proxies /api to VITE_API_TARGET
# (default http://localhost:4000), so nothing here can point a dev session at
# production or trip CORS against localhost.
#
# On Render/Vercel set it in the service environment (available at build time);
# the API must list that web origin in its own WEB_ORIGIN to allow the browser
# to read the responses.
VITE_API_URL=https://reflickmovies-api.onrender.com

# Dev-server proxy target for /api. Only read by `npm run dev`.
# VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:4000
